 "result_text": "I fixed the bad ASS timestamp in `ms_to_timestamp` in `pysubs2/substation.py`. A time that rounded up to the next second, like 39.995, used to print as `39.100`. It now carries into the seconds and prints `40.00`.\n\nThe old code split the time into hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds first, then rounded the milliseconds to centiseconds. A value of 995 ms or more rounded to 100 centiseconds and was printed as `.100` with no carry. The new code rounds the whole value to centiseconds first and splits it afterwards.\n\nI checked it with 4659995 ms (1:17:39.995), which now gives `1:17:40.00`. I didn't run the CLI on your example file or run the test suite, and I didn't add a test.",
